=2 Walkthrough
* After completing the previous quest, the {n:Nomad Moogle} will give you the option to warp to a BCNM. It is a 6-person battle against {n:Atori-Tutori}. The fight is difficult and there is **an optional, but STRONGLY recommended, sidequest** to acquire an item to enfeeble {n:Atori-Tutori} beforehand. See below for details.
** Since you can purchase multiple of these items, **just get 3**.
* The {n:Nomad Moogle} will offer to warp you to one of several BC zones once you have given him the stone. The fight is the same in every zone, so which one you pick does not matter.
** Players who have previously completed the quest can assist in the fight, but the Moogle will not warp them to the BCNM.
* Warp to one of the zones with the rest of your party.
** There are {p:Home Points|Home Point} outside each destination, if you want to use your free teleport to grab one that you haven't already.
** Additionally, {n:Domenic} in {z:Lower Jeuno} (J-7) will warp you to any of these Burning Circle zones after completing this quest.
* Fight and defeat {n:Atori-Tutori}. He is level 99 and uses Hundred Fists which removes all enfeebling effects on him.
* If you are defeated, you may enter the fight again by paying 1 Merit Point or 5 {i:High Kindred's Crests|High Kindred's Crest|2956} to the {n:Nomad Moogle}.
** Keep in mind that besides obtaining seals from mobs, two easier ways exist to obtain various seals:
*** Spend {p:Login Campaign} points - each seal is only 5 points.
*** {n:Shemo} can exchange any other type of seal at a 3:1 ratio.
* Warp back and talk to the {n:Nomad Moogle} to have your level limit increased, and to finish this quest.

=3 Sidequest
* You can get an enfeebling item ({i:Olde Rarab Tail|Olde Rarab Tail|5911}) from {p:Degenhard} in {z:Bastok Markets} (I-10). HP #4 is closest. Head south, down the stairs, and he is on the left.
** {p:Degenhard} will not accept the trade before flagging the quest Beyond Infinity.
*** Select **"But of course!"** as a response to __Accept the challenge?__ to flag the quest acceptance.
*** You can then choose **"Nowhere yet"** instead of a destination, and have the required conversation with Maat to learn about Degenhard.
** **NOTICE:** Once you have accepted the quest Beyond Infinity don't warp yet, instead talk to {p:Maat} (You may need to talk to him several times to get him to bring up 'paying a visit to {p:Degenhard}'. __If you don't do this step__ you won't be allowed to trade items to {p:Degenhard} for an {i:Olde Rarab Tail|Olde Rarab Tail|5911}.
* Talk to {p:Degenhard} {z:Bastok Markets} (I-10) (Home Point #4) at least once to hear about the items he wants (otherwise he won't accept them!).
* Trade {p:Degenhard} a {i:Seasoning Stone|Seasoning Stone|3541}, {i:Fossilized Fang|Fossilized Fang|3543}, and {i:Fossilized Bone|Fossilized Bone|3542} for an {i:Olde Rarab Tail|Olde Rarab Tail|5911}.
** These items have been available from the {p:Repeat Login Campaign} for a measly 10 points for years, with no sign that they will be removed.
** May 2025 {p:Repeat Login Campaign} removed these items, and likely will become rotating in availability by month.
** These items also drop off level 90+ monsters in specific zones.
* This item will remove {n:Atori-Tutori}'s damage taken cap (about 100 damage per hit with no Tail used) and {p:Terrorize|Terror} him for 2 minutes.
** You can get two or more and use them sequentially after the previous one wears off.

